<title>USA: First Chicago ups prime rate to 8.5 pct.</title>
<headline>First Chicago ups prime rate to 8.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Chicago NBD Corp said Wednesday it had raised its prime lending rate to 8.50 percent from 8.25, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The move follows a decision by the Federal Reserve on Tuesday to raise the federal funds rate by 25 basis points to 5.50 percent, and to leave the discount unchanged.</p>
<p>A number of other banks have also raised their prime rates to 8.50 percent.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787 ))</p>
</text>
